@node LibreClaw DSL
@section Podomation DSL

The @code{pod-cmacs-libreclaw-module} (built into temacs and
registered on cmacs's shared PodEngine at
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-start} time) exposes libreclaw events and
actions to podomation DSL rules.

@subsection Events emitted

All events use the @code{on_cm_lc_} prefix so they don't collide
with @code{pod-cmacs-module} or @code{pod-gowl-module}.

@multitable @columnfractions .4 .55
@headitem Event @tab Fires on
@item @code{on_cm_lc_message}
@tab inbound message received
@item @code{on_cm_lc_response}
@tab outbound message sent
@item @code{on_cm_lc_room_joined}
@tab channel joined a room
@item @code{on_cm_lc_room_removed}
@tab channel left a room
@item @code{on_cm_lc_channel_connected}
@tab channel connection opened
@item @code{on_cm_lc_channel_disconnected}
@tab channel connection closed
@item @code{on_cm_lc_channel_error}
@tab channel error reported
@item @code{on_cm_lc_session_created}
@tab AI session spawned
@item @code{on_cm_lc_session_destroyed}
@tab AI session reaped
@end multitable

Event payloads are @code{GVariant a@{sv@}} dicts with string-valued
keys matching libreclaw's signal argument names.

@subsection Actions supported

@multitable @columnfractions .2 .35 .4
@headitem Action @tab Arguments @tab Effect
@item @code{send_message}
@tab @code{channel}, @code{room}, @code{body}
@tab async send
@item @code{join_room}
@tab @code{channel}, @code{room}
@tab placeholder — 0.18.0
@item @code{leave_room}
@tab @code{channel}, @code{room}
@tab placeholder — 0.18.0
@end multitable

@subsection Example DSL

@example
pod lc = cmacs_libreclaw->new();

lc->on_cm_lc_message where event->body contains "@@bot"
    => cmacs_libreclaw->send_message(
         channel = event->channel_id,
         room    = event->room_id,
         body    = "You rang?");

lc->on_cm_lc_channel_error
    => cmacs->log("channel @{event->channel_id@} error: @{event->error@}");
@end example

The @code{cmacs_libreclaw} pod and the @code{cmacs} pod run on the
same engine, so pods in either can cross-reference each other.
